#!/bin/sh
snapshot="$("$HOME/.local/bin/antonina-scheduler-snapshot" 2>/dev/null || printf '{}')"
exec timeout -k 15s 900s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode-go/step-5-preview-free --variant high --dir /workspace/antonina "ANTONINA-SCHEDULER-TURN. Optimize wall-clock time by topology. Use CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.
MANDATORY MODEL: launch Antonina agents exclusively with opencode-go/step-5-preview-free (Step 5 Preview Free) using variant high; never fall back to any other model. If Step 5 is unavailable, record the blocker and return instead of substituting.
PRIORITY-FIRST DISPATCH: CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.open_issues is already in the human-set board priority order. Evaluate that order, respecting actual dependencies/ownership/topology and expected wall-clock speedup. Do NOT impose a mandatory project-breadth barrier or worker-count quota. An independent high-priority front may launch even if another project is unrepresented. Use the full issue list; do not truncate at six per project. Closed-issue agents in orphan_agents do NOT represent open work. Do not launch work against a closed issue.
Read candidate via antonina-scheduler-issue --issue ISSUE. If open and worthwhile, run antonina-scheduler-worktrees --issue ISSUE. If [] provision an isolated, registered Git worktree with antonina-scheduler-provision --issue ISSUE --json and retry worktree lookup; if provisioning cannot determine a safe repository, record the concrete blocker and scan onward. DO NOT silently skip every newly-created issue because registration is missing. No filesystem-wide workspace scans; use the authorized provisioner.
Use the atomic launch transaction: antonina-scheduler-launch --issue ISSUE --cwd CWD --title 'Project #ISSUE: task' --summary SUMMARY --prompt PROMPT --json. The launcher MUST validate issue state immediately before launch. Never launch duplicate issue work or reuse a live cwd.
The scheduler is topology-only: independent work is not a scarce slot. Launch when the marginal speedup is positive, irrespective of current number of workers; prioritize the user-set queue. AssemblyP1 has multiple independent finite-work interpretations #208–#216, so they should receive independent fronts without waiting for #217 synthesis.
FINISH THE BOUNDED TURN: after one successful launch or a precise blocker, RETURN IMMEDIATELY. The s6-supervised loop is responsible for invoking another fresh reconciliation pass. NEVER idle-watch or sleep within this turn.
CURRENT_SNAPSHOT:
$snapshot"
